target:    readme.txt
gate:      composer test:db-floor-metadata
kind:      introduce-defect
expect:    past the 300-character guideline
rationale: Appends one sentence to the 6.0.0 notice, taking it to 354 bytes; the three rollback-fact regexes still match, so only the length check can fire.
---
--- a/readme.txt
+++ b/readme.txt
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@
 == Upgrade Notice ==
 
 = 6.0.0 =
-Back up first. Adds columns/indexes and removes no rows. Older versions keep working; added columns stay. Migration steps wait for your click. Some metrics change: see changelog. Pro adds detailed heatmaps and scheduled reports.
+Back up first. Adds columns/indexes and removes no rows. Older versions keep working; added columns stay. Migration steps wait for your click. Some metrics change: see changelog. Pro adds detailed heatmaps and scheduled reports. Read the full release notes and review every migration step on wordpress.org before you begin this update. Keep a separate backup for recovery.
 
 
 == Changelog ==
